(window.DVR_PAPERS=window.DVR_PAPERS||{})["me-easy-2026-013"]={"v":1,"id":"me-easy-2026-013","title":"Mock Level Test-4 Full Syllabus GATE 2026 ME","sourceTitle":"Mock Level Test-4 Full Syllabus GATE 2026 ME","branch":"MECHANICAL ENGINEERING","code":"ME","provider":"DVRUO EASY","providerKey":"easy","series":"GATE 2026 Online Test Series - Mechanical Engineering","seriesId":"me-easy-2026","num":13,"category":"mock","year":"2026","format":"A","durationSec":10800,"info":{"meta":"Package: GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series - Mechanical Engineering • Questions: 65","package":"GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series - Mechanical Engineering"},"source":"MECHANICAL ENGINEERING/MADE EASY/GATE_2026_+_GATE_2025_Online_Test_Series_Mechanical_Engineering/025_Mock Level Test-4 Full Syllabus GATE 2026 ME.html","questions":[{"n":1,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Consider the below question followed by three statements. You have to study the question and the statements and decide which of the statement(s) is/are necessary to answer the given question.<br />\nA, B and C together start a business with a total investment of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/da/da91251fe33dbf1471e7.png\" /> At the end of the year, the total profit is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/22/2211c20705f88f1f7e1e.png\" /> What is A’s share in the profit?<br />\n1. A’s contribution is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/57/571a28b567c9698614a9.png\" /> times B’s contribution.<br />\n2. B’s contribution is twice that of C.<br />\n3. A’s contribution is thrice that of C.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 and 2 only"},{"key":"B","html":"2 and 3 only"},{"key":"C","html":"All 1, 2 and 3"},{"key":"D","html":"Any two of the three"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/91/91a49c0b45964e671d3e.png\" /></div>"},{"n":2,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Find the next term in the alpha-numerical series:<br />\nZ1A, X2D, V6G, T21J, R88M, P445P, ?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"N2676S"},{"key":"B","html":"N2676T"},{"key":"C","html":"T26TON"},{"key":"D","html":"T2676N"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c2/c24006aada2079c59084.png\" /></div>"},{"n":3,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Of the five villages P, Q, R, S and T situated close to each other, P is 1 m to the west of Q, R is 1 m to the south of P, T is 1 m to the north of Q and S is 1 m to the east of T. Then R is in which direction with respect to S?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"North-West"},{"key":"B","html":"South-East"},{"key":"C","html":"South-West"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d8/d80606359c36474cd08a.png\" /></div>"},{"n":4,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A conical vessel whose internal radius is 10 cm and height 72 cm is full of water. If this water is poured into a cylindrical vessel with internal radius 30 cm, the height of the water level rises in it is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2f/2f8d9c4280fd58a7bb01.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/81/817475010e991c937c59.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/56/563cf7cb19a824372cbd.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6b/6be0b3a7b62e983f7a1f.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":5,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>An opaque solid cone is suspendended in the path of a parallel beam of light such that its shadow is cast on a screen oriented perpendicular to the direction of the light beam.<br />\nUnder these conditions, which one of the shadows <em>A</em>, <em>B</em>, <em>C</em> and <em>D</em> is not possible?</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/3c/3c74dd8bf2da97a6b6f5.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"A"},{"key":"B","html":"B"},{"key":"C","html":"C"},{"key":"D","html":"D"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)<br />\n&bull; A cone&rsquo;s circular base can project a circle when the cone&rsquo;s axis is perpendicular to the screen.<br />\n&bull; Tilt the cone a bit and the circle becomes an ellipse.<br />\n&bull; If the cone is oriented so the apex and base edge project on the screen, the outline can form a<br />\ntriangle C the lateral surface projects as two straight sloping edges meeting at the apex.</p>"},{"n":6,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The sum of all the numbers greater than 10000 formed by using digits 0, 2, 4, 6, 8 (no digit repeated in any number) is equal to?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"5199960"},{"key":"B","html":"5209960"},{"key":"C","html":"5199980"},{"key":"D","html":"5299960"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/16/16b716747e3f8daa98d3.png\" /></div>"},{"n":7,"type":"NAT","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Monica has a piece of canvas whose area is 551 m<sup>2</sup>. She uses it to have a conical tent made, with a base radius of 7 m. Assuming that all the stitching margins and the wastage incurred while cutting, amounts to approximately 1 m2, the volume of the tent is _____ m<sup>3</sup>.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1225,1239],"answerText":"1232","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>1232 (1225 - 1239)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5d/5d44770e139a6e3f0d8b.png\" /></div>"},{"n":8,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>The diameter of a sphere is decreased by 25%. By what percentage does its curved surface area decrease?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"25%"},{"key":"B","html":"37.5%"},{"key":"C","html":"43.75%"},{"key":"D","html":"50%"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\nIf the diameter decreases by 25%, the radius also decreases by 25%.<br />\nSo the new radius = 75% of the old radius = 0.75r<br />\nCurved surface area is proportional to the square of the radius : (0.75)<sup>2</sup> = 0.5625<br />\nThis means the new area is 56.25% of the original area<br />\nSo, the decrease = 100 &ndash; 56.25 = 43.75%<br />\nTherefore, the curved surface area decreases by 43.75%.</p>"},{"n":9,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A tariff against computers made in country z is needed to protect computer manufactures in this country. With such a tariff, domestic computer manufactures would see increased sales of their own products. And increased sales frequently lead to reduced prices. The conclusion which can<br />\nbe most properly drawn from above statement is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"A lack of protective tariff has hampered computer production in this country."},{"key":"B","html":"A tariff would probably lead to a drop in prices for buyers of domestically produced computers."},{"key":"C","html":"Domestic manufacturers will decrease computer production if a protective tariff is not established"},{"key":"D","html":"A drop in computer prices is likely to create more jobs in the country."}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>"},{"n":10,"type":"NAT","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0","html":"<p>All the soldier are arranged in the form of an equivalent triangle i.e. one soldier in front row, 2 soldier in second row and 3 soldier in third row and so on. If 669 more soldiers from other are added in such a way that all the soldiers form a square and each of the side contains 8 less soldier<br />\nthan each side of equilateral triangle. The number of soldier initially were _________ .</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1540,1540],"answerText":"1540","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>1540</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/bb/bb4ebe47b4757cc09620.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":11,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Both creep resistance and tensile strength of a metal can be enhanced by</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Increase in the grain size"},{"key":"B","html":"Decrease in the grain size"},{"key":"C","html":"Addition of dispersoid"},{"key":"D","html":"Annealing"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\nThe strength and hardness in some metal alloys may be enhanced by the presence of extremely<br />\nsmall and uniformly dispersed particles within the original phase matrix by the means of dispersion<br />\nhardening. In this, dispersoids are introduced as insoluble particles as second phase particle.<br />\nSecond phase particles in the form of very small uniformly distributed particles are added to the<br />\nmatrix. These will block dislocation motion extremely well and strengthen the metal. Creep<br />\nresistance is also improved by the presence of finely dispersed intermetallic precipitates which<br />\nare stable at high temperature. Dispersoids resist the movement of dislocations that causes high<br />\ntemperature creep.</p>"},{"n":12,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>The number of dummy activities required for making the network diagram of the following project having 9 activities is</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fd/fd627af259f492a6bde9.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"0"},{"key":"B","html":"1"},{"key":"C","html":"2"},{"key":"D","html":"3"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/7b/7b6968842b0985e0cbc2.png\" /></div>"},{"n":13,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A two-dimensional velocty field is given by</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/69/692d8b3a543440b88e4b.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>If the flow is incompressible, then the constant <em>C</em> should be</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"-10"},{"key":"B","html":"0"},{"key":"C","html":"5"},{"key":"D","html":"10"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f8/f8d7d22da3d13a04e322.png\" /></div>"},{"n":14,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>For the beam shown below,</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d8/d898b71ab147dad2c6ee.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>Which of the following diagrams are discontinuous at the mid-span?</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Bending moment diagram only"},{"key":"B","html":"Axial force diagram and bending moment diagram"},{"key":"C","html":"Bending moment diagram and shear force diagram"},{"key":"D","html":"Axial force diagram, bending moment diagram and shear force diagram"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/81/813ccc3894624439fa20.png\" /></div>"},{"n":15,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Which of the following metal working operations can be categorized as an indirect compression process?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Forging"},{"key":"B","html":"Wire drawing"},{"key":"C","html":"Extrusion"},{"key":"D","html":"Stretch forming"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\nWire drawing and stretch forming - Tension<br />\nForging - Directional compression<br />\nExtrusion - Direct and indirect compression</p>"},{"n":16,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A sphere of mass 300 g is attached to an inextensible string of length 1.3 m, whose upper end is fixed to the ceiling as shown in the figure. The sphere is made to describe a horizontal circle of radius 0.5 m.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4c/4c87cb6f5068fdfb38d7.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The angular velocity of the sphere is</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"2.859 rad/sec"},{"key":"B","html":"7.23 rad/sec"},{"key":"C","html":"8.86 rad/sec"},{"key":"D","html":"10.2 rad/sec"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/21/21caf4de3fec96edd3f5.png\" /></div>"},{"n":17,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A solid shaft of mild steel 240 mm diameter is to be replaced by a hollow shaft of alloy steel for which the allowable shear stress is 22% greater. The power transmitted is increased by 20% and the speed of rotation is increased by 5%. The maximum internal diameter of the hollow shaft, if its outer diameter is equal to the diameter of the solid shaft is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"80 mm"},{"key":"B","html":"100 mm"},{"key":"C","html":"120 mm"},{"key":"D","html":"140 mm"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c6/c6bd8bdf81d334f0562d.png\" /></div>"},{"n":18,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Two gears with stub-teeth having addendum 0.84 times the module are in mesh. The tangential force is 0.95 times the total force between the gear teeth. For a gear ratio of 3, what is the minimum number of teeth on the gear pinion to avoid undercutting?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<em>T<sub>G</sub></em> = 42, <em>t<sub>p</sub></em> = 14"},{"key":"B","html":"<em>T<sub>G</sub></em> = 48, <em>t<sub>p</sub></em> = 16"},{"key":"C","html":"<em>T<sub>G</sub></em> = 51, <em>t<sub>p</sub></em> = 17"},{"key":"D","html":"<em>T<sub>G</sub></em> = 54, <em>t<sub>p</sub></em> = 18"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1f/1fc42e742d6a6a1e5553.png\" /></div>"},{"n":19,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Given for water,<br />\n• At 190°C, saturation pressure = 12.54 bar<br />\n• At 210°C, saturation pressure = 19.06 bar<br />\n• At 200°C, <em>v<sub>f</sub></em> = 1.1565 × 10<sup>–3</sup> m3/kg and <em>v<sub>g</sub></em> = 0.1274 m<sup>3</sup>/kg<br />\nUsing the Clapeyron equation, the enthalpy of vaporization of water at 200°C is approximately.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1857 kJ/kg"},{"key":"B","html":"1924 kJ/kg"},{"key":"C","html":"1947 kJ/kg"},{"key":"D","html":"2020 kJ/kg"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/03/030c8f84d1fa8f89919b.png\" /></div>"},{"n":20,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A diesel cycle in which the temperature at the end of compression is 527°C, the gravimetric air-fuel ratio is 25 : 1 and the calorific value of fuel is 40 MJ/kg. Specific heat of air at constant pressure is 1 kJ/kgK and is independent of temperature. Assume combustion product contains air only. The cut-off ratio of cycle is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"2"},{"key":"B","html":"3"},{"key":"C","html":"4"},{"key":"D","html":"5"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/db/db16fd73ce7fa31e1739.png\" /></div>"},{"n":21,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>If the eigen vectors of a 2 × 2 matrix A corresponding to the eigen values –1 and 6 are <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/98/980acf7d185391ef9da2.png\" /> and <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/01/01b6b0c31b5bafc80777.png\" /> respectively, then the matrix <em>A</em> is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/af/af575184e6f47164b95d.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d6/d6d2e82e6a2a1ea7d869.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/95/9524d380cdcbe25a9cc6.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b1/b1eb86e1b430ac9a57f2.png\" />"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/22/22476a716f3e082909ea.png\" /></div>"},{"n":22,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>The particular solution of the below differential equation is</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8a/8add511f991080966c07.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6b/6b63b2f94526247bc079.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/bc/bc2839002f170b34ad6d.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c0/c054ba4cb63c40d306e5.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c3/c3c5fe8aacd47ac668d1.png\" />"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/21/212ef07bb268689451a3.png\" /></div>"},{"n":23,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A band brake has a band width of 80 mm and wraps around a drum of diameter 300 mm. The coefficient of friction between the band and the drum is 0.2 and the angle of wrap of 270°. The brake is required to exert a friction torque of 900 Nm. The maximum tension developed in the band is _______ kN [Correct upto two decimal places]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[9.6,10.2],"answerText":"9.83","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>9.83 (9.60 - 10.20)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e9/e917112f563e28e748a1.png\" /></div>"},{"n":24,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A binary Pb-Sn alloy contains 40 wt% Sn and is maintained at a temperature of 200°C. At this temperature it contains two phases. The phases are the α solid solution of Sn in Pb containing 17 wt% Sn and the Pb-Sn liquid phase containing 55 wt% Sn. The fraction of the α-phase in the alloy is ___ %. [Correct upto one decimal place]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[39.3,39.7],"answerText":"39.5","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>39.5 (39.3 - 39.7)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e0/e028cfa62b5368cfc7fe.png\" /></div>"},{"n":25,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>According to the Naval Research Laboratory method, the shape factor of a steel slab casting having dimensions 25 × 25 × 5 cm is ______. [Rounded off to the nearest integer]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[10,10],"answerText":"10","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>10 (10 - 10)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2c/2c13bbd616bb89611d7f.png\" /></div>"},{"n":26,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>An oil with a viscosity of 0.40 Ns/m<sup>2</sup> and density 900 kg/m3 flows in a pipe of diameter, 0.02 m.<br />\nThe pipe flow velocity is 0.064 m/s. The hydrodynamic entry length is ______ mm. [Correct upto two decimal places]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[3.2,3.6],"answerText":"3.46","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>3.46 (3.20 - 3.60)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/39/39e1b31d449850b46ab2.png\" /></div>"},{"n":27,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>In a 2 litre four-stroke indirect injection diesel engine, the indicated thermal efficiency is 60%, mechanical efficiency is 85% and the volumetric efficiency is 80%. The air-fuel ratio (by mass) is 13 : 1 and the calorific value of fuel is 40 MJ/kg. The brake specific fuel consumption is _______ kg/kW-hr. [Correct upto two decimal places]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.16,0.2],"answerText":"0.18","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.18 (0.16 - 0.20)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/17/170f28da0f5dcbf3b831.png\" /></div>"},{"n":28,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>In machining tests with two tools <em>A</em> and <em>B</em>, the Taylor’s tool life equation parameters were determined as <em>n</em> = 0.45, C = 90 for tool <em>A</em> and <em>n</em> = 0.3, <em>C</em> = 60 for tool B. The cutting speed above which tool <em>A</em> will have higher tool life than tool <em>B</em> is _____ m/min. (Correct upto two decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[26.45,26.85],"answerText":"26.67","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>26.67 (26.45 - 26.85)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ff/ff19efe18d833aa4493b.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ae/aed799b6390d38ce3610.png\" /></div>"},{"n":29,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>In a Steam power plant, steam is first expands isentropically in a turbine from an initial condition of 100 bar and 500°C to a pressure of 40 bar. Then the steam is reheated up to 500°C at constant pressure. The steam is then expanded isentropically in another turbine upto a condenser pressure 0.01 bar.<br />\nThe amount of heat rejected in the condensor is _____ kJ/kg. (Correct upto two decimal places.)<br />\nFor steam, At 100 bar, 500°C: <em>h</em> = 3373.7 kJ/kg, <em>s</em> = 6.5966 kJ/kg; At 40 bar, 500°C:<br />\n<em>h</em> = 3445.3 kJ/kg, s = 7.0901 kJ/kgK and at 0.01 bar; h<sub>f</sub> = 29.3 kJ/kg, h<sub>g</sub> = 2514.2 kJ/kg, s<sub>f</sub> = 0.1059 kJ/kgK, s<sub>g</sub> = 8.9756 kJ/kgK.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1956.2,1956.9],"answerText":"1956.61","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>1956.61 (1956.20 - 1956.90)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f9/f9501853c7849ba93137.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/83/83c3d6e5862e1b81ea4f.png\" /></div>"},{"n":30,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>One end of a very long aluminium rod is connected to a wall at 140°C while the other end protrudes into a room at 15°C. The diameter of the rod is 3 mm and the heat transfer coefficient between the rod surface and environment is 300 W/m2K. If the thermal conductivity of the rod is 150 W/mK then, the total heat dissipated by the rod is _______ W. [Correct upto three decimal places]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[6.82,6.87],"answerText":"6.843","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>6.843 (6.820 - 6.870)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/73/739f7ca7f9e207c6f0c0.png\" /></div>"},{"n":31,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>Two cubical castings of the same metal are moulded in green sand have sides of 3 cm and 6 cm respectively. If the smaller casting solidifies in 2 minutes, then the expected solidification time of the larger casting is _____ minutes. [Rounded off to nearest integer]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[8,8],"answerText":"8","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>8 (8 - 8)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6c/6cd550a1723949faf607.png\" /></div>"},{"n":32,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>An aluminium specimen of gauge length 200 mm and diameter 25 mm is tested under torsion. A torque of 16.5 × 10<sup>3</sup> N-mm produces an angular twist of 0.2 degree in the specimen. The modulus of rigidity of aluminium is ______ GPa. [Correct upto two decimal places]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[24.3,24.8],"answerText":"24.65","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>24.65 (24.30 - 24.80)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c9/c9d022eb0ad5bbda8aa3.png\" /></div>"},{"n":33,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A disk is mounted on a shaft between the two bearings as shown in the figure. The disk spins anticlockwise when viewed from right hand side bearing. The shaft precesses about a vertical axis at some angular velocity ‘ω’ in clockwise direction when viewed from above. Neglect the weight of the disk.<br />\nDetermine the direction of reaction forces on the shaft end.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/70/704a73d7b4900b7c8574.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Reaction on shaft at end A will be downward"},{"key":"B","html":"Reaction on bearing at end A will be downward"},{"key":"C","html":"Reaction on shaft at end A will be upward"},{"key":"D","html":"Reaction on bearing at end A will be upward"}],"answer":["A","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/7f/7f77734f69f57054740d.png\" /></div>"},{"n":34,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A steel wire is drawn from an initial diameter of 12.7 mm to a final diameter of 10.2 mm at a speed of 90 m/min. The half cone angle of the die is 6° and the coefficient of friction at the job-die interface is 0.1.<br />\nBased on the above data which of the following options is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"The reduction in area <em>r</em> is 0.355."},{"key":"B","html":"The reduction in area <em>r</em> is 0.533."},{"key":"C","html":"The true strain is 0.438."},{"key":"D","html":"The true strain is 0.483."}],"answer":["A","C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f4/f4a54484fa52b9b54e88.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f2/f282db735bb84ea5fc4c.png\" /></div>"},{"n":35,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A random variable ‘x’ is defined by</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/88/884454cae2df1d691512.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The expected value of 2<em>x</em> + 5 is _______.</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[7,7],"answerText":"7","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>7 (7 - 7)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5f/5f470d82a975993b5dac.png\" /></div>"},{"n":36,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A vertical load W is applied to the rigid cantilever frame shown in the figure below.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ce/ce0cde3996c219b9e237.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>Assume <em>EI</em> to be constant throughout the frame and neglect axial deformations.<br />\nThe vertical displacement of the point <em>C</em> is</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/86/862a5f6f849f975ad64e.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f3/f3b08a8344d046c1d78b.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/90/907dc8897f2077266b13.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ac/ac7cf4f5920c273104b6.png\" />"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/39/39f9c890e2c0d1bb186d.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/83/83b8cd42b7fe4908c0a5.png\" /></div>"},{"n":37,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A refrigerator uses R-12 with a mass flow rate of 0.03 kg/s. The refrigerant enters the compressor as saturated vapour at 150.9 kPa. After adiabatic compression, it enters the condenser as superheated vapour at 500 kPa and 100°C. The refrigerant leaves the condenser as saturated liquid at the same pressure. The enthalpy of superheated vapour at 500 kPa and 100°C is 252.05 kJ/kg.<br />\nUse the following data:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b8/b81674d11862cb44eef7.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The COP of the cycle is</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1.25"},{"key":"B","html":"1.50"},{"key":"C","html":"1.75"},{"key":"D","html":"2.00"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a5/a58e35c64e11120ba9ee.png\" /></div>"},{"n":38,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Steam enters a counter flow heat exchanger, dry saturated at 10 bar and leaves at 350°C. The mass flow rate of steam is 800 kg/min. The hot gases enters the heat exchanger at 650°C with a mass flow rate is 1350 kg/min. If the tubes are 30 mm in diameter and 3 m long, then the number of tubes required is<br />\nNeglect the resistance offered by metallic tubes.<br />\nUse the following data:<br />\nFor steam: <em>t</em><sub>sat</sub> = 180°C(at 10 bar); c<sub>ps</sub> = 2.71 kJ/kgK; h<sub>s</sub> = 600 W/m<sup>2</sup>K<br />\nFor gas: <em>c</em><sub>pg</sub> = 1 kJ/kgK; <em>h<sub>g</sub></em> = 250 W/m<sup>2</sup>K</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"503"},{"key":"B","html":"510"},{"key":"C","html":"516"},{"key":"D","html":"524"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/bb/bbe431e8e005987b2a8e.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6a/6a2ecd99889ba54e6ca9.png\" /></div>"},{"n":39,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>At a post office stamp vendor window, customers arrive at an average rate of 20 customers every 10 minutes. The vendor clerk can serve 5 customers in 2 minute. If the clerk works an 8-hours shift, the total idle time of the clerk is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"80 min"},{"key":"B","html":"96 min"},{"key":"C","html":"120 min"},{"key":"D","html":"144 min"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/cb/cbe13a00613a5d1828e5.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/58/58a8c8baf830b8428e81.png\" /></div>"},{"n":40,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Two blocks of masses 5 kg and 3 kg are placed one over the other as shown in the figure. A horizontal force of 100 N is applied on the 5 kg block. The acceleration with which the 3 kg block will start separating from the 5 kg block is<br />\n[Take g = 10 m/s<sup>2</sup>]</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/30/3009e1d1dd7322ba97d7.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"0 m/s<sup>2</sup>"},{"key":"B","html":"10.8 m/s<sup>2</sup>"},{"key":"C","html":"2 m/s<sup>2</sup>"},{"key":"D","html":"8.8 m/s<sup>2</sup>"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/78/78acf3ae225e7d97da82.png\" /></div>"},{"n":41,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Two columns of circular cross-section one hollow and the other solid are made of the same material and have the same length, same cross-sectional area and same end conditions. The internal diameter of the hollow column is half of its external diameter. The ratio of the buckling strengths of the hollow column to the solid column is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1.66"},{"key":"B","html":"1.56"},{"key":"C","html":"1.46"},{"key":"D","html":"1.36"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a3/a307f987d41f2b3829db.png\" /></div>"},{"n":42,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The torque developed by an engine is given by T = (1800 + 350 sin2θ) N.m where θ is the angle turned by the crank from inner dead center. The engine drives a machine that requires a driving torque of (1800 + 230 sinθ) N.m. The rotating parts of the engine have a mass of 250 kg and a radius of gyration of 480 mm. If the maximum speed of rotation is 240 rpm, the power developed by the engine at the mean speed is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"39.6 kW"},{"key":"B","html":"45.24 kW"},{"key":"C","html":"54.42 kW"},{"key":"D","html":"60.92 kW"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2a/2a8e3c063ef206233fbc.png\" /></div>"},{"n":43,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>In an orthogonal cutting operation, the rake angle of the tool is 10°. The chip thickness increased by 140% as compared to uncut chip thickness. The coefficient of friction at chip-tool interface is 0.5. Find ratio of <em>F<sub>n</sub></em> to <em>F<sub>s</sub></em> where <em>F<sub>n</sub></em> is ‘backing up’ force on the chip provided by workpiece which act normal to shear plane and <em>F<sub>s</sub></em> is the resistance to shear in forming the chip.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"0.53"},{"key":"B","html":"0.80"},{"key":"C","html":"1.13"},{"key":"D","html":"0.85"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ae/ae9e3ed538333086f428.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/64/646569e802f16f187bd7.png\" /></div>"},{"n":44,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Water flows steadily through a horizontal pipeline at a volumetric flow rate of 0.5 m<sup>3</sup>/s. The inside diameter of the pipe is 0.5 m. The density and kinematic viscosity of water are 1000 kg/m<sup>3 </sup>and 10<sup>–6</sup> m<sup>2</sup>/s, respectively. The Darcy-Weisbach friction factor is 0.0093 and acceleration due to gravity is 9.81 m/s<sup>2</sup>. To maintain a constant flow rate, the power required per unit length of the pipeline is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"30.15 W/m"},{"key":"B","html":"39.64 W/m"},{"key":"C","html":"41.38 W/m"},{"key":"D","html":"55.92 W/m"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/53/53c1d43d94a3191ce4bc.png\" /></div>"},{"n":45,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The assignment problem given below requires four different jobs to be performed on four different machines. The cost <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/56/56f9c1a877f1fad278bd.png\" /> of assigning each job to each machine is shown in the table.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b7/b71b604dad5c3947624f.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The minimum cost of assignment is</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4c/4cdccada8d73eb1b1305.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/18/18642e4d4470741c25f5.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a6/a67ee44fa4f873f9bd2e.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e2/e26019e071803be84a68.png\" />"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/68/685a4bde4b715e20201e.png\" /></div>"},{"n":46,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A Francis turbine has an outer diameter of 1.4 m and rotates at 430 rpm. Water enters the runner without shock with a flow velocity of 9.5 m/s and leaves the runner without whirl with an absolute velocity of 7 m/s. The turbine develops a power of 12.25 MW and the flow rate through the turbine is 12 m<sup>3</sup>/s. The absolute velocity of water at entry to the runner is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"33.75 m/s"},{"key":"B","html":"43.75 m/s"},{"key":"C","html":"32.39 m/s"},{"key":"D","html":"42.39 m/s"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/13/13fabb0db62fa1d585cb.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/32/3271c4b8d9d915ea0228.png\" /></div>"},{"n":47,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>The directional derivative of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/b8/b8159b909534ef432042.png\" /> at the point <em>P</em>(1, 2, –1) along <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/2e/2efe0d1c45ad9f0dd263.png\" /> is ________. (Correct upto three decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[-6.6,-6.4],"answerText":"-6.532","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>-6.532 (-6.600 - -6.400)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/eb/eb8ebe8d749e690b54ce.png\" /></div>"},{"n":48,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>If <em>f</em> (<em>x</em>) = 12<em>x</em><sup>5</sup> – 45<em>x</em><sup>4</sup> – 20<em>x</em><sup>3</sup> + 90<em>x</em><sup>2</sup>, then</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"The minimum value of the function <em>f</em>(<em>x</em>) is –459."},{"key":"B","html":"The maximum value of the function <em>f</em> (<em>x</em>) is 53."},{"key":"C","html":"<em>f</em> (<em>x</em>) has neither a maximum nor a minimum at <em>x</em> = –1."},{"key":"D","html":"<em>f</em> (<em>x</em>) has neither a maximum nor a minimum at <em>x</em> = 3."}],"answer":["A","B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/aa/aa72b80a88dc1af51542.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9e/9e79bf5c9baafff22f6d.png\" /></div>"},{"n":49,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A bracket is attached to a column by means of four identical rivets and it is subjected to an eccentric load of 12 kN as shown in the figure. If the permissible shear stress is 60 MPa then the design diameter of the rivets will be ______ mm [Correct upto two decimal places]</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/32/32eb0459ab52d74a4e7b.png\" /></div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[15.75,16.15],"answerText":"15.96","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>15.96 (15.75 - 16.15)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1b/1bab222801ed5c611304.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c5/c5a9d20efaa95cd5c239.png\" /></div>"},{"n":50,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>In the mechanism shown in the figure, the angular velocity of link AB is 3 rad/sec.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/77/773fd045182828a873d3.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The angular velocity of link CD is ____ rad/s. [Correct upto two decimal places]</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[3.1,3.4],"answerText":"3.25","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>3.25 (3.10 - 3.40)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/aa/aa6031b3c9c549e1b373.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/60/60e481833ca7b2634a32.png\" /></div>"},{"n":51,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Air in a piston-cylinder arrangement is heated at constant pressure by a heat addition of 100 kJ/kg of air. Initially the air is at 28°C while the surrounding is at 21°C. The change in availability of the air is _____ kJ/kg [Correct upto two decimal places].<br />\n[Take <em>c</em><sub><em>p</em>,air</sub> = 1.005 kJ/kgK and atmospheric air pressure as 1 bar]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[15.35,15.85],"answerText":"15.66","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>15.66 (15.35 - 15.85)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/0e/0eea62dfdd7a8a01f255.png\" /></div>"},{"n":52,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Given the following linear programming problem,</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/46/46681ceb9f6293cc81ab.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The corner point of a feasible region for which z is maximum is given as (<em>x</em><sub>1</sub>, <em>x</em><sub>2</sub>). The value of <em>x</em><sub>1</sub> is _____ (Correct upto two decimal places)</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[2.1,2.4],"answerText":"2.25","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>2.25 (2.10 - 2.40)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ac/ac377695fcadbc56d3d3.png\" /></div>"},{"n":53,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A flat plate, 1 m wide and 1.5 m long is maintained at uniform surface temperature of 90°C and is exposed to an air stream at a free stream temperature of 10°C. The rate of energy dissipation from the plate is 0.375 kW. Air flow over the flat plate along the 1.5 m length. Assuming laminar flow the velocity of air is ______cm/s. [Rounded off to nearest integer] Properties of air at 50°C :<br />\nρ = 1.09 kg/m<sup>3</sup>, k = 0.028 W/mK, c<sub>p</sub> = 1.007 kJ/kgK, μ = 2.03 × 10<sup>–5</sup> kg/ms, Pr = 0.7</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[99,101],"answerText":"100","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>100 (99 - 101)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b3/b3c30d3515bef21e78a9.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/55/55d4f4ccdc4f19684755.png\" /></div>"},{"n":54,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A spring mass damper system has a damping factor of 0.30. The frequency ratio at which the system attains peak amplitude is ______. [Correct upto three decimal places]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.901,0.912],"answerText":"0.906","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.906 (0.901 - 0.912)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/45/4532c3e188fc6857fb7f.png\" /></div>"},{"n":55,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A two stage air compressor with intercooling is used in a gas turbine power plant. Air enters the compressor at 1 bar and 27°C. The maximum temperature of the cycle is limited to 900°C and the maximum pressure ratio is 6. If the temperature of air after intercooling is 47°C, the intermediate pressure, for minimum work input to compressor between the stages is ______ bar. [Correct upto two decimal places]<br />\n[Take adiabatic index, γ<sub>air</sub> = 1.4]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[2.5,2.9],"answerText":"2.74","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>2.74 (2.50 - 2.90)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/03/03e8dd387a1b2abe36c5.png\" /></div>"},{"n":56,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A cantilever beam of length 2 m carries a uniformly distributed load 2 kN/m over a length of 1 m from the free end and a point load of 1 kN at the free end. The slope at the free end of the cantilever is _______ degrees. [Correct upto three decimal places]<br />\n[Take, <em>E</em> = 210 GPa and <em>I</em> = 6.667 × 10<sup>7</sup> mm<sup>4</sup>]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.016,0.02],"answerText":"0.018","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.018 (0.016 - 0.020)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/53/53eacd691823329d13b1.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e5/e5c835200dca83e50d73.png\" /></div>"},{"n":57,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>An ideal gas undergoes a cyclic process consisting of the following three processes:<br />\nProcess 1-2: Compression process with PV = Constant<br />\nProcess 2-3: Constant pressure process<br />\nProcess 3-1: Constant volume process<br />\nFor process 3-1 the change in internal energy <em>U</em><sub>3</sub> – <em>U</em><sub>1</sub> = 3549 kJ<br />\nChanges in kinetic and potential energies are neglected.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ed/ed29616ba905994c4eb2.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The heat transferred during the process 2-3 is ______ kJ. [Rounded off to nearest integer]</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[4665,4675],"answerText":"4669","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>4669 (4665 - 4675)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ea/ea937002f2f244ced48f.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1f/1f0432c21869d6a2634b.png\" /></div>"},{"n":58,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A metal sheet is rolled to minimum possible thickness of 2.5 mm in a single pass using rollers of diameter 300 mm without any change in its width. The friction coefficient at the work-roll interface is 0.1. The maximum possible thickness of sheet that can be rolled in a single pass is _____ mm.<br />\n[Correct upto one decimal place]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[3.9,4.1],"answerText":"4.0","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>4.0 (3.9 - 4.1)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/db/dbf329252da810a99e38.png\" /></div>"},{"n":59,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>The crank and the connecting rod lengths of a vertical single cylinder gas engine running at 2000 rpm are 60 mm and 240 mm respectively. The diameter of the piston is 80 mm, and the mass of reciprocating parts is 2 kg. At a point during power stroke the piston has moved 35.7 mm from the top dead center position. The pressure acting on the piston at this instant is 800 kN/m<sup>2</sup>. The net force acting on the piston is ______ kN. [Correct upto two decimal places]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[2.03,2.1],"answerText":"2.07","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>2.07(2.03 - 2.10)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a6/a622b703572611cffec7.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b0/b0acbfd8349e3069e92a.png\" /></div>"},{"n":60,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Two 1.2 mm thick, flat copper sheets (ρ = 9000 kg/m3 and specific heat capacity = 0.3936 kJ/kg-K) are being spot welded using a current of 6000 A for a duration of 0.18s. The electrodes used are 5 mm in diameter and have an effective resistance of 150 μΩ. Assuming that the heat generated is completely confined to the volume of material directly between the two electrodes and the temperature distribution is uniform, the temperature rise of the coper sheet is _______°C. (Correct upto two decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[5818.73,5825.72],"answerText":"5822.73","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>5822.73 (5818.73 - 5825.72)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/42/4221a33a2a95fec5caba.png\" /></div>"},{"n":61,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A solid circular bar of 50 mm diameter is subjected to torsion in a testing machine as shown in the figure. When the applied torque reaches 500 Nm, a strain gauge mounted at 45° to the axis of the bar record a strain of 339 × 10<sup>–6</sup>.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/85/85bda6b5154d48fa484e.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>Based on above information which of the following options is/are correct?</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"The shear strain at θ = 45° is 6.78 × 10<sup>–4</sup>."},{"key":"B","html":"The value of shear modulus is 60 GPa."},{"key":"C","html":"The value of shear modulus is 30 GPa."},{"key":"D","html":"The shear strain at θ = 45° is 3.39 × 10<sup>–4</sup>."}],"answer":["A","C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ea/eaaf548fb299cb5c7092.png\" /></div>"},{"n":62,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Air at 27°C and 1 bar flows over a flat plate at a speed of 2 m/s. Assuming a cubic velocity profile and the dynamic viscosity of air at 27°C to be 19.8 × 10<sup>–6</sup> kg/ms. At a distance of 400 mm from the leading edge of the plate. Which of the following statements is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"The boundary layer thickness is 0.0932 m."},{"key":"B","html":"The boundary layer thickness is 0.00857 m."},{"key":"C","html":"The mass flow rate per unit width of the plate is 0.745 kg/min."},{"key":"D","html":"The mass flow rate per unit width of the plate is 0.012 kg/min."}],"answer":["B","C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B, C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(b, c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e6/e603fef7777b10b0af24.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2e/2eeb4265ad1162951951.png\" /></div>"},{"n":63,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider an analytic function <em>f</em>(<em>z</em>) = <em>u</em> + iν, if it is given than⎥ <em>f</em>(z)⎥ is a constant, then which of the following statements are true?</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b4/b4df5897a93bfb3ae823.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"(i) and (ii) only"},{"key":"B","html":"(i) and (iii) only"},{"key":"C","html":"(ii) and (ii) only"},{"key":"D","html":"all are correct"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5b/5b1e31546a55ecd7231c.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/42/426d5aab235aa7313bb3.png\" /></div>"},{"n":64,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A function <em>f</em> (<em>x</em>) is defined as <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/88/88afaa72819e89507f8e.png\" /></p>\n\n<p>For <em>f</em>(<em>x</em>) to be a valid probability density function, the value of <em>A</em> must be</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"8"},{"key":"B","html":"16"},{"key":"C","html":"18"},{"key":"D","html":"22"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d2/d29c3102b65d442f0835.png\" /></div>"},{"n":65,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>If the residue of the function <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/e2/e2d0632f6d70d9c0858d.png\" /> then the value of <em>p</em> is ______. </p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1.8,2.2],"answerText":"2","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>2 (1.8 - 2.2)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/17/1740a6fdd4cd8a11ed68.png\" /></div>"}],"math":false,"scoring":"marks","sections":[{"name":"General Aptitude","start":0,"count":10},{"name":"Technical","start":10,"count":55}],"stats":{"questions":65,"maxMarks":100,"types":{"MCQ":33,"NAT":27,"MSQ":5},"withoutKey":0}};
